1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.450
Maya navigation
Alt + mouse, F, Home, double click

2
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:08.883
With Navigation on, in the Setup panel or in the preferences, the viewport handles like Maya's.

3
00:00:08.933 --> 00:00:14.317
Alt + left button orbits around the selection…

4
00:00:14.367 --> 00:00:19.750
…Alt + middle button pans, Alt + right button zooms in and out towards the pointer.

5
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:25.183
F frames the selection, in Object Mode and in Edit Mode on the components. Home frames everything: Maya's A (on a laptop Fn + Left Arrow).

6
00:00:25.233 --> 00:00:30.617
Double click selects an edge loop, Ctrl + double click a ring: in Blender they were Alt+click, which now orbits.

7
00:00:30.667 --> 00:00:36.050
The switch also sets Orbit Around Selection, Auto Depth and Zoom to Mouse Position. Blender's own middle-button navigation keeps working.

8
00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:41.483
Off, or with Landfall uninstalled, everything goes back to Blender's factory preferences.

9
00:00:41.533 --> 00:00:44.417
Maya navigation

